`helm upgrade --install orders ./charts/orders -n shop` started failing in CI this morning:

```
Error: UPGRADE FAILED: cannot patch "orders" with kind Deployment: Deployment.apps "orders" is invalid: spec.selector: Invalid value: v1.LabelSelector{MatchLabels:map[string]string{"app.kubernetes.io/instance":"orders", "app.kubernetes.io/name":"orders", "app.kubernetes.io/version":"5.2.0"}, MatchExpressions:[]v1.LabelSelectorRequirement(nil)}: field is immutable
```

The same PR bumped `appVersion` from 5.1.4 to 5.2.0, bumped the Kubernetes cluster from 1.30 to 1.31 last week, and refactored `_helpers.tpl` so the label helpers share code:

```
{{- define "orders.selectorLabels" -}}
app.kubernetes.io/name: {{ include "orders.name" . }}
app.kubernetes.io/instance: {{ .Release.Name }}
app.kubernetes.io/version: {{ .Chart.AppVersion | quote }}
{{- end }}

{{- define "orders.labels" -}}
helm.sh/chart: {{ include "orders.chart" . }}
{{ include "orders.selectorLabels" . }}
app.kubernetes.io/managed-by: {{ .Release.Service }}
{{- end }}
```

My teammate thinks the 1.31 upgrade tightened validation and wants to pin the API version. Another wants to just add `--force` to the CI command. What's actually wrong and what's the fix?

Our monorepo has a Go service in `/` and its Helm chart in `charts/relay`. release-please creates release PRs fine and bumps `version.go`, but it never bumps `charts/relay/Chart.yaml` `version`/`appVersion`, and the CHANGELOG has `ci:` and `chore(deps):` commits sitting under a "Breaking Changes" heading even though none are breaking. Files:

`.github/workflows/release.yaml`:
```yaml
- uses: googleapis/release-please-action@v4
  with:
    release-type: go
    token: ${{ secrets.RELEASE_TOKEN }}
```

`release-please-config.json`:
```json
{
  "packages": {
    ".": {
      "release-type": "go",
      "extra-files": [
        {"type": "generic", "path": "charts/relay/Chart.yaml"}
      ],
      "changelog-sections": [
        {"type": "feat", "section": "Features"},
        {"type": "fix", "section": "Bug Fixes"},
        {"type": "ci", "section": "CI", "hidden": true},
        {"type": "chore", "section": "Miscellaneous", "hidden": true}
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

`Chart.yaml` has `version: 0.9.2 # x-release-please-version` and `appVersion: "0.9.2" # x-release-please-version`. The config looks right to me. Why are both problems happening?
